          <td><code>ragu import &lt;file&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Import session data from a JSON file or URL.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>ragu upgrade [target]</code></td>
          <td>
            Upgrade to the latest release or a specific version target. The install method is
            detected automatically and the upgrade runs through it (npm, yarn, pnpm, bun, brew,
            choco, scoop, or the standalone installer); override it with
            <code>--method</code>. On Windows a standalone install cannot overwrite the binary
            that is running the command, so the new version is staged and swapped in once the
            command exits.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>ragu uninstall</code></td>
          <td>
            Remove ragu. Flags: <code>--keep-config</code>, <code>--keep-data</code>,
            <code>--dry-run</code>, <code>--force</code>.
          </td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>OpenTelemetry (OTLP) and live telemetry</h3>
    <p>
      ragu ships a small observability layer that exports Effect spans over OTLP and publishes
      them on the bus for the live TUI panel. See <a href="/docs/observability">Observability</a>
      for the full reference. Quick reference:
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      # Export to a local Jaeger collector
      OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318 ragu run "summarize this repo"

      # Disable the live panel but keep OTLP export
      OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318 \
      RAGU_DISABLE_OTEL_LIVE=1 \
      ragu serve --port 4096
    </DocCode>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      ragu doctor
      ragu doctor --json
      ragu heap --detailed
      ragu stats
      ragu usage
      ragu export abc123 > session.json
      ragu import ./session.json
      ragu upgrade
      ragu uninstall --keep-config --dry-run
    </DocCode>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
